  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nWith winds becoming light early this morning and abundant\nmoisture from previous rainfall, widespread dense fog is \nexpected. Motorists should allow extra time for the morning\ncommute. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nDrier air behind a cold front will bring dry weather for today\nand Friday. \n\nA moisture starved reinforcing cold front will push through on \nSaturday, but most of the area will remain dry. The dry weather\nwill continue on Sunday. \n\nYet another moisture starved reinforcing cold front will push\nthrough on Monday, although a few showers or thunderstorms can\nnot be ruled out. \n\nMostly dry weather will then return for Tuesday and Wednesday. \n\nWith the drier air behind these fronts, nighttime temperatures \nwill be considerably cooler, with readings generally in the 40s\nand 50s.",
